Subject: block rows: the switch as the stock fix_swtbls leaves it

The first RAM-disk boot (rd1, both lines) refused the ramdisk's row 20
as in use.  At boot the stock fix_swtbls gives every bdevsw row whose
flag lacks D_NOBRKUP the breakup gen_strategy and keeps the row's own
strategy in shadowbsw, so an empty row is gen_strategy over nodev, which
bempty took for a used one.  bempty now knows that shape; a module's
row goes in the same way (without D_NOBRKUP its strategy to shadowbsw
behind gen_strategy, with it direct); a removal puts both back.  The
state harness has the stock switch and the ramdisk's shape from the
arena.

--- a/dlm_slot.c
+++ b/dlm_slot.c
@@ -442,14 +442,26 @@
  * first-open trampoline, so a block driver's row is filled when the
  * module links, and only a pinned module may have one: the row then
  * stays until the kernel halts.  A failed load puts the row back.
+ *
+ * The switch is not as the image has it: at boot the stock fix_swtbls
+ * gives every row whose flag lacks D_NOBRKUP the breakup gen_strategy,
+ * the row's own strategy kept in shadowbsw.  So an empty row is
+ * gen_strategy over nodev, and a module's row is installed the same way:
+ * without D_NOBRKUP its strategy goes to shadowbsw behind gen_strategy.
  */
 #define	BSLOT_MAX	8
+#ifndef D_NOBRKUP
+#define	D_NOBRKUP	0x10		/* sys/conf.h: no breakup needed */
+#endif
+extern struct bdevsw shadowbsw[];
+extern int gen_strategy();
 #define	bfn(bp)	((int (**)())&(bp)->d_open)
 
 static struct dlm_bslot {
 	struct dlm_mod	*bs_mod;	/* 0: free */
 	int		bs_major;
 	struct bdevsw	bs_old;		/* the row before */
+	int		(*bs_shadow)();	/* its shadowbsw strategy before */
 } dlm_bslot[BSLOT_MAX];
 
 static struct dlm_bslot *
